    {
      "@id": "diag:t:2",
      "@type": "Ambiguity",
      "blocking": true,
      "statement": "The word 'may' in line 8 is ambiguous between a deontic reading (permission with an upper bound) and an alethic reading (a factual statement about system capacity).",
      "evidence": [
        "sf:3cece84900befdfb78d57490"
      ],
      "status": "open",
      "raisedBy": "transformer",
      "interpretations": [
        "A member is permitted to hold up to five loans at any one time, making holding more than five a prohibited action (deontic permission with a ceiling).",
        "The system is factually capable of associating at most five loans with a member at any one time (a description of a natural or technical limit, not a rule)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "diag:t:3",
      "@type": "UnresolvedReference",
      "blocking": true,
      "statement": "The complete rules governing assignment of membership numbers are delegated to Annex C, which is not present in this section; the actual assignment logic cannot be asserted from the text supplied.",
